Multi-Agent AI Research System
An AI-powered research application built with Python and LangChain that coordinates specialized agents to search the web, extract information, generate a structured research report, and evaluate the report with feedback.
Overview
Research often involves several repetitive steps: finding relevant sources, reading web pages, organizing information, writing a report, and reviewing the result. This project explores how an agent-based workflow can coordinate those steps into one pipeline.

Instead of relying on a single model call to perform the entire task, the application separates research into specialized stages and passes the results between them. A supervisor function manages the order of execution and shares state between the stages.
Note: The description below is based on the project workflow shown in the development tutorial. Confirm the exact filenames, providers, and implemented features against your local code before publishing.

Workflow
                  Research Topic
                        |
                        v
                 Research Pipeline
                        |
                        v
                   Search Agent
              (find relevant sources)
                        |
                        v
                   Reader Agent
             (extract page information)
                        |
                        v
                   Writer Chain
              (create a research report)
                        |
                        v
                   Critic Chain
            (score report and give feedback)
                        |
                        v
                  Final Research
                     Report
The pipeline coordinates the stages and passes their outputs through a shared state. The exact behaviour depends on the implementation and configuration in the code.
Main Components
1. Search Agent
Uses a web-search tool to find information relevant to the research topic.
2. Reader Agent
Uses a URL-scraping tool to retrieve and extract readable content from selected web pages.
3. Writer Chain
Uses a language model and an output parser to organize the collected research into a structured report.
4. Critic Chain
Reviews the generated report and returns a score and feedback. Treat this as an AI-assisted review, not a guarantee that every claim is correct.
5. Research Pipeline
Coordinates the components, passes results between stages using shared state, and presents the workflow output.
Why Use a Multi-Agent Workflow?
A multi-agent workflow can make a complex task easier to organize by giving individual stages clearly defined responsibilities. It can also make components easier to modify or evaluate independently.

This approach is not automatically better than using one LLM. It may increase latency, token usage, and API costs. Its value depends on whether separating the work improves the quality, reliability, or maintainability of the result for the intended task.
Technology Stack
Based on the tutorial workflow, the project involves:
- Python — application logic
- LangChain — connecting language models, prompts, tools, and output parsers
- LLM API — report generation and review (use the provider configured in your code)
- Web-search tool — finding relevant pages (use the provider configured in your code)
- Web scraping — extracting readable content from URLs
- Environment variables — configuring API credentials
Check requirements.txt and your Python files to confirm the exact libraries and providers used.
